.TH FLARESPEED 1 2026-10-24 "flarespeed 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
flarespeed \- measure internet speed against Cloudflare's network
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B flarespeed
.RB [ \-duration
.IR time ]
.RB [ \-streams
.IR n ]
.RB [ \-pings
.IR n ]
.RB [ \-json ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B flarespeed
measures the latency, jitter, download and upload speed of an internet
connection against Cloudflare's speed test service at
.IR speed.cloudflare.com ,
using the nearest Cloudflare data center.
.PP
When standard output is a terminal it shows a live view: one card each for
ping, download and upload, and a chart of the test in progress.
The view is drawn in place below the prompt and stays on screen as a
summary when the program exits.
Otherwise, or with
.BR \-json ,
it runs the test silently and prints the results as JSON.
.PP
A run has three steps:
.TP
.B Latency
The time to first byte of an empty download on a warm connection, minus the
processing time the server reports in its
.B Server-Timing
header.
The median of the samples is reported, along with jitter, the mean
difference between consecutive samples.
.TP
.B Download and upload
Several HTTP/1.1 connections transfer 25\~MB requests back to back for the
chosen duration.
The first 20% of the test (at most 2 seconds), while connections ramp up,
is left out of the reported rate.
.TP
.B Loaded latency
While each transfer test saturates the link, latency is sampled every
250\~ms.
Loaded latency much higher than idle latency means the connection suffers
from bufferbloat.
.SH OPTIONS
Options can start with one dash or two, and take their value either as the
next argument or after an equals sign.
.TP
.BI \-duration " time"
How long to run each of the download and upload tests, as a number with a
unit such as
.BR 10s ,
.B 1m30s
or
.BR 2.5m .
The default is 10s and the minimum 2s.
.TP
.BI \-streams " n"
The number of parallel connections in each direction, from 1 to 1000.
The default is 6.
.TP
.BI \-pings " n"
The number of idle latency samples, at least 2.
The default is 20.
.TP
.B \-json
Print the results as JSON instead of showing the live view.
This is the default when standard output is not a terminal.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-help
Show a summary of the options.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B r
Run the test again.
.TP
.BR q ", " Esc ", " Ctrl+C
Quit, leaving the results on screen.
.SH JSON OUTPUT
The report is an object with these members:
.TP
.B server
The Cloudflare data center:
.B colo
(its IATA airport code) and
.BR city .
Absent if the data center could not be identified.
.TP
.B client
The connection being tested:
.BR ip ,
.BR asn ,
.B org
(the network's name),
.B city
and
.BR country .
Absent along with
.BR server .
.TP
.B latency
.BR median_ms ,
.BR jitter_ms ,
.B min_ms
and
.BR max_ms .
.TP
.BR download ", " upload
.B mbps
(megabits per second),
.B bytes
(the total transferred) and
.B loaded_latency_ms
(the median latency while the link was saturated, or 0 if none was
measured).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.BR HTTPS_PROXY ", " https_proxy ", " NO_PROXY
Proxy settings, as for
.BR curl (1).
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
If set to a true value (1, t, true), the live view uses no colors.
.TP
.BR CLICOLOR ", " CLICOLOR_FORCE
Ask for colors even where they would not be used otherwise.
.TP
.BR TERM ", " COLORTERM
Used, together with the terminfo database and
.B tmux info
inside
.BR tmux (1),
to choose between truecolor, 256-color and 16-color output.
.TP
.B FLARESPEED_BASE_URL
Test against another server implementing the same endpoints
.RB ( /meta ,
.B /__down
and
.BR /__up )
instead of https://speed.cloudflare.com.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 if the test completed, 1 if it failed or was interrupted, and 2 for an
invalid command line.
.SH EXAMPLES
Run a longer test:
.PP
.RS
.B flarespeed \-duration 30s
.RE
.PP
Print just the download speed:
.PP
.RS
.B flarespeed \-json | jq .download.mbps
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR curl (1)
